@prefix :       <#> .
@prefix schema: <http://schema.org/> .
@prefix onto:   <https://www.openlinksw.com/ontology/studio#> .
@prefix rdfs:   <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

: a schema:CreativeWork ;
    schema:about :footerSparqlExplorerGate .

:footerSparqlExplorerGate a schema:HowTo ;
    schema:name "Footer SPARQL Explorer Gate"@en ;
    schema:description "Rules governing the mandatory footer SPARQL explorer section in HTML infographics: sparqlBtn presence, SAMPLE query visibility, left-alignment, and stale interactive workbench cleanup."@en ;
    schema:dateCreated "2026-06-25T00:00:00Z" ;
    schema:dateModified "2026-06-25T00:00:00Z" ;
    schema:step
        :gate-sparqlBtnMandatory,
        :gate-sparqlExplorerVisibleText,
        :gate-footerTextAlignCascade,
        :gate-staleWorkbenchCleanup,
        :gate-sparqlSectionsClosedAccordion,
        :gate-priorTemplateStalenessCheck .

# ── Gate 1: sparqlBtn is mandatory ───────────────────────────────────────────────

:gate-sparqlBtnMandatory a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 1 ;
    schema:name "sparqlBtn is a mandatory harness element — never remove in cleanup"@en ;
    schema:text """grep -n 'id=\"sparqlBtn\"' {file} — must match exactly once, inside <footer>.
If the match is absent but buildSparqlBtnHref / setSparqlFmt JS functions exist: the element was accidentally removed — restore it.

Distinction: the 4-accordion SPARQL workbench section and the footer sparqlBtn serve different purposes.
- 4-accordion: recipe queries (features, FAQ, glossary, howto)
- sparqlBtn: SAMPLE-based entity-type summary query — a required, independent deliverable

Removing a 'duplicate' SPARQL section means removing an unlabelled second copy of the accordion section, NOT the footer sparqlBtn block."""@en .

# ── Gate 2: SAMPLE query text must be visible ─────────────────────────────────────

:gate-sparqlExplorerVisibleText a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 2 ;
    schema:name "id='sparql-explorer' must display SAMPLE query as visible <pre class='sparql-code'>"@en ;
    schema:text """Encoding the SAMPLE query only inside sparqlBtn.href is insufficient — users cannot read or copy it from a URL attribute.

Required HTML structure in footer:
  <div id="sparql-explorer" class="footer-sparql-cta" style="...;text-align:left">
    <h3>Explore Knowledge Graph using SPARQL</h3>
    <p>...description...</p>
    <div class="sparql-block">
      <div class="sparql-block-hdr">
        <span class="sparql-lang-badge">SPARQL</span>
        <button class="sparql-copy-btn" onclick="copySparqlExplorer(this)">Copy</button>
      </div>
      <pre class="sparql-code" id="sparql-explorer-code">...syntax-highlighted query...</pre>
    </div>
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:16px">
      <div class="fmt-tabs">...</div>
      <a id="sparqlBtn" class="footer-sparql-btn" href="..." target="_blank">▶ Run Query</a>
    </div>
  </div>

Canonical SAMPLE query projections (never substitute):
  ?type, (SAMPLE(?s) AS ?sampleEntity), (SAMPLE(?label) AS ?sampleLabel), (COUNT(?s) AS ?entityCount)
  WHERE { GRAPH <{DAV-IRI}> { ?s rdf:type ?type . OPTIONAL { ?s rdfs:label ?label } } }
  GROUP BY ?type ORDER BY DESC(?entityCount)

Beautification pattern (established 2026-06-25):
  Syntax tokens: .sk (keywords, var(--accent)), .sf (aggregates, #9c6bde), .sv (variables, #51cf66),
                 .si (IRIs, #ff922b), .sp (prefix names, var(--muted))
  IRI angle brackets: always HTML-escaped as &lt; and &gt;
  copySparqlExplorer() must be exposed on window (defined inside D3 IIFE)."""@en .

# ── Gate 3: footer text-align:center cascade ─────────────────────────────────────

:gate-footerTextAlignCascade a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 3 ;
    schema:name "Override footer text-align:center cascade on the explorer div"@en ;
    schema:text """When footer { text-align:center } is in the CSS (common for attribution grids):

1. id="sparql-explorer" div MUST have text-align:left in its inline style.
2. .fmt-tabs CSS MUST use justify-content:flex-start (not justify-content:center).

Verification:
  grep -n 'fmt-tabs' {file} — must show justify-content:flex-start
  grep -n 'id=\"sparql-explorer\"' {file} — must show text-align:left in the style attribute

The footer text-align:center is intentional for the attribution grid; overriding it only on
the explorer section keeps both correct without touching the global rule."""@en .

# ── Gate 4: stale interactive workbench cleanup ──────────────────────────────────

:gate-staleWorkbenchCleanup a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 4 ;
    schema:name "Removing interactive workbench HTML requires removing companion JS and CSS"@en ;
    schema:text """When the interactive SPARQL workbench (textarea + recipe selector + mode buttons) is removed from HTML:

JS to remove:
  const sparqlRecipes = { ... }
  function loadSparqlRecipe(key)
  function setSparqlMode(mode, btn)
  function runSparqlQuery()
  window.loadSparqlRecipe = loadSparqlRecipe
  window.setSparqlMode = setSparqlMode
  window.runSparqlQuery = runSparqlQuery
  document.getElementById("sparqlRecipe").value = "features"  ← throws null-ref on DOMContentLoaded

CSS to remove:
  .sparql-form, .sparql-row, .sparql-row label, .sparql-input, .sparql-select,
  .sparql-textarea, .sparql-run-row, .sparql-mode-btns, .sparql-mode-btn, .sparql-mode-btn.active

CSS to KEEP (still used by accordion section and footer explorer):
  .sparql-code, .sparql-run-btn, .sparql-format-note, .sparql-wb-title, .sparql-wb-sub,
  .sparql-block, .sparql-block-hdr, .sparql-lang-badge, .sparql-copy-btn,
  .fmt-tabs, .fmt-tab-btn, .footer-sparql-cta, .footer-sparql-btn

Incident (2026-06-25): HTML removed, JS/CSS left behind. document.getElementById("sparqlRecipe")
threw null-ref on every page load; ~200 bytes of dead CSS remained."""@en .

# ── Gate 5: SPARQL-bearing sections are closed-by-default accordions ─────────────

:gate-sparqlSectionsClosedAccordion a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 5 ;
    schema:name "Any SPARQL-bearing section (sample query cards, the whole KG Explorer / SPARQL Workbench sections) must be a closed-by-default accordion"@en ;
    schema:text """Two separate levels, both required:

1. Per-query cards (schema:SoftwareSourceCode SPARQL examples rendered by build_sample_query_cards
   in html_assembler.py): each is a <details class="sparql-card"> with the resolver-linked query
   name as <summary>, no `open` attribute. SKILL.md already said "render as a <details>/<summary>
   accordion" before this fix — the generator had silently implemented plain always-open <div>
   cards instead. Same contract-vs-implementation gap pattern as generator-script-output-not-a-
   substitute-for-contract-check.ttl; verified by re-running the actual generator, not by reading
   SKILL.md prose.

2. Whole sections (#kg-explorer, #sparql-explorer): each wrapped in an OUTER
   <details class="section-accordion" id="{section}-accordion"><summary class="section-accordion-
   summary">{Title}</summary> ... existing <section id="{section}">...</section> unchanged ...
   </details>. Wrap without renaming the inner section/div ids — #kg-explorer is reused by both an
   outer <section> and an inner <div> (pre-existing duplicate-id smell, not introduced by this fix
   and not worth touching here); renaming risks breaking every CSS/JS reference
   (#kg-explorer.kg-active, getElementById('kg-explorer'), the KG Explorer POST-WRITE grep gate
   strings) for a cosmetic ID cleanup. Wrapping from the outside costs nothing and touches nothing
   else.

Required companions to the section-level wrap:
  - CSS: .section-accordion-summary chevron/hover styling (Show ▼ / Hide ▲ via [open] state).
  - JS: a same-page-anchor auto-reveal handler (hashchange + on load) that walks up .closest('details')
    from the target element and sets .open = true, then re-scrolls — otherwise clicking a nav link to
    #kg-explorer or #sparql-explorer scrolls to a collapsed, seemingly-empty area.
  - Validator: require '<details class="section-accordion" id="kg-explorer-accordion">' and the
    sparql-explorer equivalent; forbid_regex for an `open` attribute on either.

Verification:
  grep -c '<details class="sparql-card"' {file}                — ≥ 1 per SPARQL query example
  grep -c '<details class="section-accordion" id="kg-explorer-accordion">' {file}      — 1
  grep -c '<details class="section-accordion" id="sparql-explorer-accordion">' {file}  — 1
  grep -n '<details class="section-accordion"[^>]*open' {file} — must be EMPTY (closed by default)

Related bug caught in the same pass, same file (scripts/templates/styles.css): the CSS rule
`.sparql-actions a{display:inline-flex}` silently overrode the `hidden` attribute on the
legitimately-hidden #sparqlLiveLink proxy anchor, because a class selector beats a plain
attribute selector `[hidden]` on specificity regardless of source order. Any future `hidden`
element inside a styled container needs an explicit `.container [hidden]{display:none!important}`
rule — `hidden` alone is not safe once a sibling-matching class rule sets `display`.

Also removed in the same pass: a `#sparqlRun` button whose click handler was a byte-for-byte
duplicate of `#sparqlBtn` (`window.open(sparqlBtn.href)`) — a second visible "Run" control doing
the exact same thing as the first. Caught by the user noticing three "Run"-labeled controls in a
delivered artifact; only two were ever meant to be visible (#sparqlBtn + the hidden #sparqlLiveLink
proxy used by per-card Execute buttons)."""@en .

# ── Gate 6: a copied prior-HTML template must be checked against the current numbered gates ──

:gate-priorTemplateStalenessCheck a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 6 ;
    schema:name "Verify a prior HTML file is actually current before copying it as a structural base — date/grep it against the footer/about-merge, explorer-placement, and card-uniformity gates"@en ;
    schema:text """Incident (2026-08-13): enterprise-ai-coordinate-system-claude_sonnet_5-1.html was hand-built by copying uber-adr-agentic-ai-security-claude_sonnet_5-1.html (2026-08-04) as its CSS/JS/structural base. The copied file predated three later fixes and silently reintroduced all three: a standalone 'About This Page' section duplicating the footer attribution block (should have been merged per Step 186 / gate-noSecondAttributionSurface-equivalent), the SPARQL explorer stranded at the end of the footer instead of directly following #kg-explorer-section (Step 189), and unequal-width format-tab buttons / tech-cards from an unconstrained footer container (Steps 191-193). validate-harness-contract.py stayed green throughout — it checks for required CONTENT strings, not document ORDER or structural redundancy, so a passing validator run is not evidence the template is current.

Required check before treating any prior HTML file as a copy-from base:
  1. grep -c 'id=\"about\"' {template} — the match must be on the <footer> tag itself (merged), never on a separate <section id=\"about\"> that precedes </div><!-- /.page -->.
  2. Confirm the <section> immediately following id=\"kg-explorer-section\" is id=\"sparql-explorer\" — not faq/glossary/howto. If the SPARQL block lives inside <footer>, the template is stale.
  3. grep -n '.tech-card{' and '.kg-format-tabs button{' — confirm flex-centering/min-height on cards and flex:1 on tab buttons. Bare `text-align:center;padding` with no min-height, or auto-width tab buttons, means the template predates the uniformity fix.
  4. If any check fails, do not patch just the new artifact and move on — port the corrected pattern from the newest compliant file in the same output folder, and prefer it as the new copy-from baseline going forward.

'Same model, reasonably recent filename' is not sufficient evidence of compliance — only the four checks above are. This is the same underlying failure mode as Step 184 (prior-artifact-footer-polish-gate), one level earlier: that gate assumes the artifact you opened IS current; this gate makes you prove it before you copy from it."""@en .
